Same capacity (b bits), two parameterisations. (3000 steps)

   n    b   predicted    onehot      bits
------------------------------------------
   2    2     success     0.757     1.000
   3    3     success     0.498     1.000
   4    4     success     0.545     1.000
   3    2        FAIL     0.516     0.752
   4    3        FAIL     0.782     0.748

  Capacity is identical down each pair of columns; only trainability
  differs. The b=n rows are where the two diverge, and those are
  exactly the rows that decide whether the bound looks tight.
  Neither parameterisation ever succeeds below the diagonal, which is
  the only direction that could refute a lower bound.
ALLDONE
